{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the people of the king's provinces.</b> Even the people know this." "<b>One.</b> It is the king's law for all, to put to death. The word לבד always comes with a mem, whether after it or before it, except for לבד מאחד, and it is only in you that we mention Your name. [n: This comment is textually obscure; the grammatical generalization about לבד and the liturgical allusion appear compressed and possibly truncated or corrupt, and are translated hyper-literally.]" "<b>Hold out.</b> Aramaic translation-language, like ישלח, and it has no cognate in Scripture." "<b>Scepter.</b> A quadriliteral word, and the meaning is בשבט. Some say the resh is added, like the resh of שרשרת, but this is not correct, for resh is not among the servile letters; rather it is doubled, like the doubling of peh in נאפופיה and also resh in סגריר."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:59.425044731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}